3. What is the purpose of the sed command? Justify with proper example. (C01)
The sed (Stream Editor) command is used for parsing and transforming text. It works by applying a specified set of editing commands to an input stream or file, often used for powerful find-and-replace operations.
Example (Substitution):
# Finds every occurrence of 'old' and replaces it with 'new' globally in the file
sed 's/old/new/g' original_file.txt


